660 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1520 0 R
/E (My findings show that machine learning models, particularly XGBoost, can detect pediatric diabetes risk with relatively high accuracy and recall. Unlike earlier studies such as Daniel et al. \(2024\), which reported overall detection without subgroup analysis, this study demonstrates how model performance varies across gender, age, ethnicity, and insurance type.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [495]
>>
endobj
661 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1521 0 R
/E (This subgroup-specific insight allows clinicians to identify populations that may be underrepresented or underdiagnosed in EHR-based predictions, enabling more equitable and targeted screening. For example, patients from groups with historically lower data coverage \(e.g., certain age or ethnic groups\) could receive additional monitoring or laboratory testing.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [496]
>>
endobj
